Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:43:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] perf(kda): gfx938 wu LDS layouts without the bank
 conflicts of five phases (P-938bc4)

hipprof per phase (dev skip-mask build) and a ds_read_m32x16 pattern microbench
(8 lanes per cycle, grouped by lane bits 1 ^ 4, 3, 5) give a bank model that
reproduces every phase.  Layout-only changes, gfx938 only (gfx936 assembly
unchanged):
- kbT slab: granule XOR 2 ((r >> 4) & 7) (padded) / low nibble ^ 4 ((r >> 4) & 3)
  (L16): the w-MMAC B reads become conflict-free, the column fill keeps its 2-way
  minimum;
- B-form tile: granule XOR also takes element bits 6..7 (Wb C-fragment stores
  4-way -> conflict-free);
- saved-h staging: granule XOR 2 (k1 ^ k2) + k3 (ds_read_m reads conflict-free,
  staging stores 4-way -> 2-way);
- L16 natural vb rows: granule XOR 2 (j & 1) + 4 ((j >> 2) & 1) (u-MMAC
  ds_read_m 4-way -> conflict-free).
Conflicts per CTA 4096 -> 1280 (padded), 8704 -> 768 (L16).  VGPR 124 -> 128 /
128, no scratch, LDS unchanged.  Gate 84/84 bit-identical.  wu 1.008-1.086x
(median of 3 ABBA runs, 9 shapes).  With P-938bc2, mk3_fb ABBA x2: bwd
1.002-1.021x, fwd+bwd 1.001-1.017x (geomean 1.006).

